            "creation_time": "2026-06-05T07:49:36Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 3726\ndef=function(...) { standardGeneric(...) } gets braces removed\n\nThere's been conventional wisdom aroud for a while to \"just omit the braces when writing standard generic\":\n\n```\n# DO THIS\nsetGeneric(\"f1\", function(...) standardGeneric(\"f1\"))\n\n# DON'T DO THIS\nsetGeneric(\"f2\", function(...) { standardGeneric(\"f2\") })\n```\n\nE.g. this wound up in the Tidyverse style guide [1] for a long time (since refactored).\n\n`?setGeneric` is mum on the issue, but the scuttlebutt (see the comment thread in [1]) was \"there's a performance implication\". Upon investigation [2], this is not _really_ true -- compiled (e.g. package) code has no performance difference, but there _is_ a small overhead to using `{` in interactive code, which I intuit is rare.\n\nPerformance aside, I think this is hard to reason about:\n\n```\nsetGeneric(\"f1\", function(obj) standardGeneric(\"f1\"))\nsetGeneric(\"f2\", function(obj) { standardGeneric(\"f2\") })\nis(getGeneric(\"f1\"))\n# [1] \"standardGeneric\"  \"genericFunction\"  \"function\"         \"OptionalFunction\" \"PossibleMethod\"   \"optionalMethod\"  \nis(getGeneric(\"f2\"))\n# [1] \"nonstandardGenericFunction\" \"genericFunction\"            \"nonstandardGeneric\"         \"function\"                   \"OptionalFunction\"           \"PossibleMethod\"            \n# [7] \"optionalMethod\"\n```\n\n'nonstandardGenericFunction', AIUI, is meant for more complicated functions that do non-trivial things (e.g. argument validation [3]), but some branch of which includes `standardGeneric()`; simple `{` wrapping need _not_ fall under this heading.\n\nOne further motivation for changing this is to simplify downstream authors' lives -- `{` can be used for standardization and readability, if appropriate [4].\n\n---\n\nThe proposed patch strips away this issue by teaching `setGeneric()` to look for simple `{`-wrapped `standardGeneric()` and to strip the `{` away. This removes any performance overhead and makes the resulting generic inherit from `standardGeneric`.\n\nI'm not perfectly happy with the proposed approach, which encountered two clunky issues:\n\n - `body()` retains srcref attributes for braced functions, but not unbraced ones:\n\n    ```\n    options(keep.source=TRUE) # force for batch sessions\n    is.null(attributes(body(function(x) x)))\n    # [1] TRUE\n    is.null(attributes(body(function(x) {x} )))\n    # [1] FALSE\n    ```\n\n - `identical(ignore.srcref=TRUE)` does not apply to the `body()` of a closure, only the closure itself:\n\n    ```\n    options(keep.source=TRUE)\n    f1 = function(x) { x }\n    f2 = function(x) {\n      x\n    }\n    identical(f1, f2)\n    # [1] TRUE\n    identical(body(f1), body(f2))\n    # [1] FALSE\n    ```\n\nHence, `attributes(fbody) <- NULL`.\n\n\n [1] https://github.com/hadley/adv-r/issues/1804\n [2] https://github.com/r-lib/lintr/issues/1968#issuecomment-4626931684\n [3] https://github.com/cran/copula/blob/d0ddd79049170bad2dfd243f86bb483e91c3108f/R/margCopula.R#L11-L15\n [4] https://github.com/posit-dev/air/issues/398",
